v 3
d 'RTMTOOLS': Stata tools for the design and weighting of real-time monitoring phone surveys
d
d rtmtools gives task teams Stata commands with dialog boxes (User > RTM tools) for
d the weights of a phone panel round (base weights; nonresponse and attrition
d adjustment by weighting classes, response propensity, entropy balancing or cell
d post-stratification; trimming; calibration to population totals; household weights
d from person weights; weighting report), for design-based estimates, for sample
d sizes, allocation across strata and probability draws from a frame, and for frames
d of areas (list frames; grid frames from a population raster and boundaries, with
d replacement cells and splits; spatially spread draws). Every run is exported (manifest, CSV tables, an Excel display workbook
d and a dashboard page that read the export and compute nothing). The weighting
d steps run through svycal, svyset, logit, survwgt, ipfraking and ebalance, the
d frame steps through shp2dta and geoinpoly; nothing in the package uses R.
d Listing support (rtmlist): listing forms with segmentation and the completed listing
d checked into the household frame. Portable do-file versions of the four workflows
d (package rtmtools_portable, net get) can be copied and adapted by another program following ADAPTATION.md.
d Method defaults cite the HFPS sampling guidelines (Himelein et al. 2020), the
d Listening to Tajikistan methods report, Ambel et al. 2021 and UN 2008.
d
d KW: survey weights
d KW: calibration
d KW: nonresponse adjustment
d KW: entropy balancing
d KW: phone survey
d KW: real-time monitoring
d
d Requires: Stata version 16 (svycal: Stata 18); survwgt, ebalance, ipfraking, gsample, moremata, shp2dta and geoinpoly from SSC for the corresponding steps
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261025
d
d Author: Real-Time Monitoring Survey Handbook task team, World Bank
d
